.TH B34ST 1 "June 2026" "B34ST 0.3.0" "Operator Tools"
.SH NAME
B34ST \- guided control plane for FBR34KER research workflows
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B B34ST
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B B34ST
is the canonical operator entry point for the project. With no arguments it
opens a session-logged guided control panel covering builds, tests, QEMU,
external authorized first-stage execution, FBRI images, next-stage loading,
deployment, modules, runtime console access, modification evidence, physical
validation, and release packaging.
.PP
Firmware workflows include target-specific IPSW discovery, Apple-hosted
downloads, signed update or erase-restore execution, and tethered downgrade
plans delegated to an external authorized boot adapter.
.PP
The initial dashboard displays the connected product, mode, board, reviewed
launch firmware, current firmware when available, latest signed firmware,
matching profiles, and device-specific available or blocked actions.
.PP
Target-changing operations require explicit authorization. Runtime
modification and jailbreak states are evidence-gated and are not inferred
from transport success or textual monitor output.
.PP
The installed executable uses uppercase
.B B34ST
because the source package directory is named
.IR b34st ;
case-insensitive filesystems cannot safely provide both names.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B control-panel
Open the guided operator interface.
.TP
.B research-runtime
Run the exact-target, evidence-gated physical research-runtime orchestrator.
.TP
.B environment-plan
Create a bounded simulation or research-runtime plan.
.TP
.B validate-session
Validate a recorded session bundle.
.TP
.B physical-validation
Generate or inspect physical-validation evidence.
.TP
.B hardware-prepare
Generate read-only hardware preparation material.
.TP
.BI "fbr34ker " arguments
Run a lower-level FBR34KER backend command.
.SH SOURCE TREE
From the unpacked source tree, run:
.PP
.RS
.B ./scripts/B34ST
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fbr34ker (1)
